<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP January coal output up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP January coal output up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd said on Tuesday its production of coal in Queensland rose 14 percent in January to 2.0 million tonnes from a year earlier because of a better performance from the Peak Downs preparation plant.</p>
<p>Year-to-date output for the eight months to January 31, saw an 11 percent rise year-on-year to 15.43 million tonnes, BHP said.</p>
<p>January coal shipments rose to meet increased customer demand and the commencement of full prouduction at Mt Owen in October last year, BHP said.  </p>
<p>It said iron ore output in Western Australia fell 12 percent in January to 3.9 million tonnes due to train cancellations and wet ore handling caused by poor weather at the Mount Newman and Goldsworthy mines.</p>
